ALL.append(q(400,"Medium",'"Bravo! You have done an excellent job," the director told the team.',["The director congratulated the team on having done an excellent job.","The director told the team that bravo they have done an excellent job.","The director told the team that you have done an excellent job.","The director told the team that they had done an excellent job."],"The director congratulated the team on having done an excellent job.","Exclamation of praise: 'Bravo' → congratulated + on + -ing; natural indirect form.",["exclamation","reporting verb","gerund"]))

# ===================== HARD (401-500) =====================

ALL.append(q(401,"Hard",'"I have been informed that the department will be undergoing a major restructuring, and I want to assure you that your positions are secure," the secretary told the employees at the general assembly.',["The secretary told the employees at the general assembly that she had been informed that the department would be undergoing a major restructuring and that she wanted to assure them that their positions were secure.","The secretary told the employees that she has been informed that the department will be undergoing a major restructuring and she wants to assure them that their positions are secure.","The secretary told the employees that she had been informed that the department would be undergoing a major restructuring and that she wanted to assure you that your positions were secure.","The secretary told the employees that she had been informed that the department will be undergoing a major restructuring and that she wanted to assure them that their positions were secure."],"The secretary told the employees at the general assembly that she had been informed that the department would be undergoing a major restructuring and that she wanted to assure them that their positions were secure.","Multiple backshifts: 'have been informed' → 'had been informed'; 'will be' → 'would be'; 'want' → 'wanted'; 'are' → 'were'; 'I' → 'she'; 'you/your' → 'them/their.'",["tense backshift","compound sentence","pronoun change"]))
ALL.append(q(402,"Hard",'"Had I known about the policy change earlier, I would have adjusted my proposal accordingly, but nobody informed me until it was too late," the frustrated contractor said to the procurement officer.',["The frustrated contractor told the procurement officer that had he known about the policy change earlier, he would have adjusted his proposal accordingly, but nobody had informed him until it had been too late.","The frustrated contractor told the procurement officer that if he had known about the policy change earlier, he would have adjusted his proposal accordingly, but nobody had informed him until it had been too late.","The frustrated contractor told the procurement officer that had I known about the policy change earlier, I would have adjusted my proposal accordingly, but nobody informed me until it was too late.","The frustrated contractor told the procurement officer that if he had known about the policy change earlier, he would have adjusted his proposal accordingly, but nobody informed him until it was too late."],"The frustrated contractor told the procurement officer that if he had known about the policy change earlier, he would have adjusted his proposal accordingly, but nobody had informed him until it had been too late.","Type 3 conditional stays; 'informed' → 'had informed'; 'was' → 'had been'; 'I' → 'he'; 'my' → 'his'; 'me' → 'him.'",["conditional","tense backshift","compound sentence"]))
ALL.append(q(403,"Hard",'"Not only have I submitted all the required documents, but I have also completed the mandatory training that was supposed to be finished by next month," she told the evaluator.',["She told the evaluator that not only had she submitted all the required documents, but she had also completed the mandatory training that had been supposed to be finished by the following month.","She told the evaluator that not only has she submitted all the required documents, but she has also completed the mandatory training that was supposed to be finished by next month.","She told the evaluator that not only had she submitted all the required documents, but she had also completed the mandatory training that was supposed to be finished by the following month.","She told the evaluator that not only had I submitted all the required documents, but I had also completed the mandatory training."],"She told the evaluator that not only had she submitted all the required documents, but she had also completed the mandatory training that had been supposed to be finished by the following month.","'Have submitted' → 'had submitted'; 'have completed' → 'had completed'; 'was supposed' → 'had been supposed'; 'I' → 'she'; 'next month' → 'the following month.'",["tense backshift","compound sentence","time expression"]))
ALL.append(q(404,"Hard",'"I would appreciate it if you could look into this matter at your earliest convenience and let me know what steps are being taken to resolve the issue," the complainant wrote in his letter to the ombudsman.',["The complainant wrote to the ombudsman that he would appreciate it if they could look into that matter at their earliest convenience and let him know what steps were being taken to resolve the issue.","The complainant wrote to the ombudsman that he would appreciate it if you could look into this matter at your earliest convenience and let me know what steps are being taken.","The complainant wrote that he would appreciated it if they could look into that matter at their earliest convenience.","The complainant wrote to the ombudsman that he will appreciate it if they can look into that matter."],"The complainant wrote to the ombudsman that he would appreciate it if they could look into that matter at their earliest convenience and let him know what steps were being taken to resolve the issue.","'Would' stays; 'could' stays; 'are being taken' → 'were being taken'; 'I' → 'he'; 'you/your' → 'they/their'; 'me' → 'him'; 'this' → 'that.'",["no tense change","passive voice","pronoun change"]))
ALL.append(q(405,"Hard",'"The committee has unanimously decided that the project shall proceed as planned, provided that all environmental impact assessments have been satisfactorily completed," the chairperson announced at the press conference.',["The chairperson announced at the press conference that the committee had unanimously decided that the project should proceed as planned, provided that all environmental impact assessments had been satisfactorily completed.","The chairperson announced that the committee has unanimously decided that the project shall proceed as planned, provided that all environmental impact assessments have been satisfactorily completed.","The chairperson announced that the committee had unanimously decided that the project shall proceed as planned, provided that all environmental impact assessments had been satisfactorily completed.","The chairperson announced that the committee had unanimously decided that the project should proceed as planned, provided that all environmental impact assessments have been satisfactorily completed."],"The chairperson announced at the press conference that the committee had unanimously decided that the project should proceed as planned, provided that all environmental impact assessments had been satisfactorily completed.","'Has decided' → 'had decided'; 'shall' → 'should'; 'have been completed' → 'had been completed.'",["tense backshift","modal verb","embedded clause"]))
ALL.append(q(406,"Hard",'"Why didn\'t anyone inform me that the regulations had been amended before I submitted my application, which was based entirely on the old guidelines?" the aggrieved applicant demanded to know.',["The aggrieved applicant demanded to know why nobody had informed him that the regulations had been amended before he had submitted his application, which had been based entirely on the old guidelines.","The aggrieved applicant demanded to know why didn't anyone inform him that the regulations had been amended before he submitted his application.","The aggrieved applicant demanded to know why nobody informed him that the regulations had been amended before he submitted his application, which was based entirely on the old guidelines.","The aggrieved applicant demanded to know why nobody had informed me that the regulations had been amended before I had submitted my application."],"The aggrieved applicant demanded to know why nobody had informed him that the regulations had been amended before he had submitted his application, which had been based entirely on the old guidelines.","'Didn't inform' → 'hadn't informed'; 'submitted' → 'had submitted'; 'was based' → 'had been based'; 'me/I/my' → 'him/he/his.'",["wh-question","tense backshift","compound sentence"]))
ALL.append(q(407,"Hard",'"I am writing to formally request that the investigation be reopened in light of the new evidence that has recently come to our attention," the lawyer stated in his motion.',["The lawyer stated in his motion that he was writing to formally request that the investigation be reopened in light of the new evidence that had recently come to their attention.","The lawyer stated that he is writing to formally request that the investigation be reopened in light of the new evidence that has recently come to their attention.","The lawyer stated that he was writing to formally request that the investigation was reopened in light of the new evidence that had recently come to their attention.","The lawyer stated that I was writing to formally request that the investigation be reopened in light of the new evidence that had recently come to our attention."],"The lawyer stated in his motion that he was writing to formally request that the investigation be reopened in light of the new evidence that had recently come to their attention.","'Am writing' → 'was writing'; subjunctive 'be reopened' stays; 'has come' → 'had come'; 'I' → 'he'; 'our' → 'their.'",["tense backshift","subjunctive","formal reporting"]))
ALL.append(q(408,"Hard",'"I must confess that I have been having second thoughts about the merger ever since the financial audit revealed several discrepancies that had not been previously disclosed to the board," the CEO admitted during the closed-door meeting.',["The CEO admitted during the closed-door meeting that he had to confess that he had been having second thoughts about the merger ever since the financial audit had revealed several discrepancies that had not been previously disclosed to the board.","The CEO admitted that he must confess that he has been having second thoughts about the merger ever since the financial audit revealed several discrepancies.","The CEO admitted that he had to confess that he had been having second thoughts about the merger ever since the financial audit had revealed several discrepancies that had not been previously disclosed to the board.","The CEO admitted that I must confess that I have been having second thoughts about the merger."],"The CEO admitted during the closed-door meeting that he had to confess that he had been having second thoughts about the merger ever since the financial audit had revealed several discrepancies that had not been previously disclosed to the board.","'Must' → 'had to'; 'have been having' → 'had been having'; 'revealed' → 'had revealed'; 'I' → 'he.'",["tense backshift","modal verb","compound sentence"]))
ALL.append(q(409,"Hard",'"If the government does not act swiftly to address the concerns of the affected communities, I fear that the situation will deteriorate further and may lead to civil unrest," the senator warned during the plenary session.',["The senator warned during the plenary session that if the government did not act swiftly to address the concerns of the affected communities, he feared that the situation would deteriorate further and might lead to civil unrest.","The senator warned that if the government does not act swiftly, he fears that the situation will deteriorate further and may lead to civil unrest.","The senator warned that if the government did not act swiftly, he feared that the situation would deteriorate further and may lead to civil unrest.","The senator warned that if the government did not act swiftly to address the concerns of the affected communities, I feared that the situation would deteriorate further and might lead to civil unrest."],"The senator warned during the plenary session that if the government did not act swiftly to address the concerns of the affected communities, he feared that the situation would deteriorate further and might lead to civil unrest.","'Does not act' → 'did not act'; 'fear' → 'feared'; 'will' → 'would'; 'may' → 'might'; 'I' → 'he.'",["tense backshift","conditional","modal verb"]))
ALL.append(q(410,"Hard",'"I have always maintained that transparency and accountability are the cornerstones of good governance, and I will continue to advocate for these principles regardless of the political consequences," the commissioner declared.',["The commissioner declared that he had always maintained that transparency and accountability were the cornerstones of good governance and that he would continue to advocate for those principles regardless of the political consequences.","The commissioner declared that he has always maintained that transparency and accountability are the cornerstones of good governance and he will continue to advocate for these principles.","The commissioner declared that he had always maintained that transparency and accountability are the cornerstones of good governance and that he would continue to advocate for those principles.","The commissioner declared that I had always maintained that transparency and accountability were the cornerstones of good governance."],"The commissioner declared that he had always maintained that transparency and accountability were the cornerstones of good governance and that he would continue to advocate for those principles regardless of the political consequences.","'Have maintained' → 'had maintained'; 'are' → 'were'; 'will continue' → 'would continue'; 'I' → 'he'; 'these' → 'those.'",["tense backshift","compound sentence","place expression"]))

ALL.append(q(411,"Hard",'Which of the following correctly converts this to indirect speech: "I shall ensure that every citizen who has been displaced by the calamity receives adequate assistance from the government," the president promised.',["The president promised that he would ensure that every citizen who had been displaced by the calamity received adequate assistance from the government.","The president promised that he shall ensure that every citizen who has been displaced by the calamity receives adequate assistance from the government.","The president promised that he would ensure that every citizen who had been displaced by the calamity receives adequate assistance from the government.","The president promised that he would ensure that every citizen who has been displaced by the calamity received adequate assistance from the government."],"The president promised that he would ensure that every citizen who had been displaced by the calamity received adequate assistance from the government.","'Shall ensure' → 'would ensure'; 'has been displaced' → 'had been displaced'; 'receives' → 'received'; 'I' → 'he.'",["tense backshift","embedded clause","modal verb"]))
ALL.append(q(412,"Hard",'"I cannot understand why the department has not yet implemented the reforms that were approved by the legislature more than two years ago," the oversight committee chair said in frustration.',["The oversight committee chair said in frustration that she could not understand why the department had not yet implemented the reforms that had been approved by the legislature more than two years before.","The oversight committee chair said that she cannot understand why the department has not yet implemented the reforms that were approved by the legislature more than two years ago.","The oversight committee chair said that she could not understand why the department had not yet implemented the reforms that were approved by the legislature more than two years ago.","The oversight committee chair said that she could not understand why the department has not yet implemented the reforms that had been approved by the legislature more than two years before."],"The oversight committee chair said in frustration that she could not understand why the department had not yet implemented the reforms that had been approved by the legislature more than two years before.","'Cannot' → 'could not'; 'has not implemented' → 'had not implemented'; 'were approved' → 'had been approved'; 'ago' → 'before'; 'I' → 'she.'",["tense backshift","time expression","embedded clause"]))
ALL.append(q(413,"Hard",'"Not only did the contractor fail to meet the deadline, but he also submitted substandard work that does not comply with the specifications outlined in the contract," the project engineer reported to the management committee.',["The project engineer reported to the management committee that not only had the contractor failed to meet the deadline, but he had also submitted substandard work that did not comply with the specifications outlined in the contract.","The project engineer reported that not only did the contractor fail to meet the deadline, but he also submitted substandard work that does not comply with the specifications.","The project engineer reported that not only had the contractor failed to meet the deadline, but he also submitted substandard work that does not comply with the specifications outlined in the contract.","The project engineer reported that not only had the contractor failed to meet the deadline, but he had also submitted substandard work that did not comply with the specifications."],"The project engineer reported to the management committee that not only had the contractor failed to meet the deadline, but he had also submitted substandard work that did not comply with the specifications outlined in the contract.","'Did fail' → 'had failed'; 'submitted' → 'had submitted'; 'does not comply' → 'did not comply.'",["tense backshift","compound sentence","negative statement"]))
ALL.append(q(414,"Hard",'"I would like to know whether the allegations that have been leveled against my client are supported by any concrete evidence, or whether this is merely a politically motivated witch hunt," the defense lawyer asked the prosecutor.',["The defense lawyer asked the prosecutor whether the allegations that had been leveled against his client were supported by any concrete evidence, or whether it was merely a politically motivated witch hunt.","The defense lawyer asked the prosecutor whether the allegations that have been leveled against his client are supported by any concrete evidence, or whether this is merely a politically motivated witch hunt.","The defense lawyer asked the prosecutor whether the allegations that had been leveled against my client were supported by any concrete evidence, or whether this was merely a politically motivated witch hunt.","The defense lawyer asked the prosecutor if the allegations that had been leveled against his client were supported by any concrete evidence, or if it was merely a politically motivated witch hunt."],"The defense lawyer asked the prosecutor whether the allegations that had been leveled against his client were supported by any concrete evidence, or whether it was merely a politically motivated witch hunt.","'Have been leveled' → 'had been leveled'; 'are supported' → 'were supported'; 'is' → 'was'; 'my' → 'his'; 'this' → 'it.'",["tense backshift","yes/no question","embedded clause"]))
ALL.append(q(415,"Hard",'"I am deeply concerned that the funds that were allocated for the infrastructure project have been diverted to other purposes without proper authorization from the oversight committee," the auditor general stated in his report.',["The auditor general stated in his report that he was deeply concerned that the funds that had been allocated for the infrastructure project had been diverted to other purposes without proper authorization from the oversight committee.","The auditor general stated that he is deeply concerned that the funds that were allocated for the infrastructure project have been diverted to other purposes.","The auditor general stated that he was deeply concerned that the funds that were allocated for the infrastructure project had been diverted to other purposes without proper authorization.","The auditor general stated that he was deeply concerned that the funds that had been allocated for the infrastructure project have been diverted to other purposes."],"The auditor general stated in his report that he was deeply concerned that the funds that had been allocated for the infrastructure project had been diverted to other purposes without proper authorization from the oversight committee.","'Am concerned' → 'was concerned'; 'were allocated' → 'had been allocated'; 'have been diverted' → 'had been diverted'; 'I' → 'he.'",["tense backshift","passive voice","embedded clause"]))
ALL.append(q(416,"Hard",'Identify the error: The witness testified that he has seen the accused enter the building at 9 PM the previous night.',["Error: 'has seen' should be 'had seen' (past perfect required after past reporting verb 'testified').",  "There is no error in this sentence.","Error: 'the previous night' should be 'last night.'","Error: 'testified' should be 'testifies.'"],"Error: 'has seen' should be 'had seen' (past perfect required after past reporting verb 'testified').","When the reporting verb is past ('testified'), present perfect must backshift to past perfect.",["error recognition","tense backshift","present perfect"]))
ALL.append(q(417,"Hard",'Identify the error: She asked me where did I put the documents that she had given me.',["Error: 'where did I put' retains inverted order. Correct: 'where I had put.'","There is no error.","Error: 'had given' should be 'gave.'","Error: 'me' should be 'I.'"],"Error: 'where did I put' retains inverted order. Correct: 'where I had put.'","Indirect questions require normal word order and removal of 'did.' Also 'put' should backshift to 'had put.'",["error recognition","word order","tense backshift"]))
ALL.append(q(418,"Hard",'Identify the error: He said me that he would not be able to attend the conference the following week.',["Error: 'said me' is incorrect. Should be 'told me' or 'said to me.'","There is no error.","Error: 'would not' should be 'will not.'","Error: 'the following week' should be 'next week.'"],"Error: 'said me' is incorrect. Should be 'told me' or 'said to me.'","'Said' cannot take a direct personal object. Use 'told + person' or 'said to + person.'",["error recognition","reporting verb","grammar rule"]))
ALL.append(q(419,"Hard",'Identify the error: The manager told the staff that they should submitted their reports before the deadline.',["Error: 'should submitted' is incorrect. Should be 'should submit' (modal + base form).", "There is no error.","Error: 'told' should be 'said.'","Error: 'their' should be 'your.'"],"Error: 'should submitted' is incorrect. Should be 'should submit' (modal + base form).","Modal verbs are always followed by the base form of the verb, never the past participle.",["error recognition","modal verb","grammar rule"]))
ALL.append(q(420,"Hard",'Identify the error: She asked that whether I had completed the assignment.',["Error: 'that whether' is redundant. Use either 'asked whether' or 'asked if,' not both with 'that.'","There is no error.","Error: 'had completed' should be 'have completed.'","Error: 'I' should be 'she.'"],"Error: 'that whether' is redundant. Use either 'asked whether' or 'asked if,' not both with 'that.'","For indirect yes/no questions, use 'if' or 'whether' alone. 'That' is not used with questions.",["error recognition","conjunction","yes/no question"]))

ALL.append(q(421,"Hard",'Identify the error: The director ordered the employees to must wear their IDs at all times.',["Error: 'to must wear' is incorrect. After 'ordered + person + to,' use base verb: 'to wear.' No modal after 'to.'","There is no error.","Error: 'ordered' should be 'told.'","Error: 'their' should be 'your.'"],"Error: 'to must wear' is incorrect. After 'ordered + person + to,' use base verb: 'to wear.' No modal after 'to.'","The infinitive structure (to + base verb) cannot include a modal. 'Ordered them to wear' is correct.",["error recognition","infinitive structure","modal verb"]))
ALL.append(q(422,"Hard",'Choose the BEST indirect form for this complex statement: "I have been trying to contact you since Monday, but your phone has been switched off, and the emails I sent have all bounced back," he complained to the IT department.',["He complained to the IT department that he had been trying to contact them since Monday, but their phone had been switched off, and the emails he had sent had all bounced back.","He complained to the IT department that he has been trying to contact them since Monday, but their phone has been switched off, and the emails he sent have all bounced back.","He complained to the IT department that he had been trying to contact you since Monday, but your phone had been switched off, and the emails I sent had all bounced back.","He complained to the IT department that he had been trying to contact them since Monday, but their phone had been switched off, and the emails he sent all bounced back."],"He complained to the IT department that he had been trying to contact them since Monday, but their phone had been switched off, and the emails he had sent had all bounced back.","All present perfects → past perfects; 'I' → 'he'; 'you/your' → 'them/their'; 'sent' → 'had sent.'",["tense backshift","compound sentence","pronoun change"]))
ALL.append(q(423,"Hard",'"I strongly urge the committee to reconsider its decision, which I believe was made without due consideration of all the relevant facts and circumstances that have since come to light," the petitioner said.',["The petitioner said that he strongly urged the committee to reconsider its decision, which he believed had been made without due consideration of all the relevant facts and circumstances that had since come to light.","The petitioner said that he strongly urges the committee to reconsider its decision, which he believes was made without due consideration.","The petitioner said that he strongly urged the committee to reconsider its decision, which he believed was made without due consideration of all the relevant facts and circumstances that have since come to light.","The petitioner said that I strongly urge the committee to reconsider its decision."],"The petitioner said that he strongly urged the committee to reconsider its decision, which he believed had been made without due consideration of all the relevant facts and circumstances that had since come to light.","'Urge' → 'urged'; 'believe' → 'believed'; 'was made' → 'had been made'; 'have come' → 'had come'; 'I' → 'he.'",["tense backshift","embedded clause","formal reporting"]))
ALL.append(q(424,"Hard",'"Neither the complainant nor the respondent has provided sufficient documentary evidence to support their respective claims, and I therefore recommend that the case be dismissed for lack of merit," the investigating officer concluded.',["The investigating officer concluded that neither the complainant nor the respondent had provided sufficient documentary evidence to support their respective claims and that he therefore recommended that the case be dismissed for lack of merit.","The investigating officer concluded that neither the complainant nor the respondent has provided sufficient documentary evidence and he therefore recommends that the case be dismissed.","The investigating officer concluded that neither the complainant nor the respondent had provided sufficient documentary evidence and that he therefore recommended that the case was dismissed for lack of merit.","The investigating officer concluded that neither the complainant nor the respondent had provided sufficient documentary evidence and I therefore recommend that the case be dismissed."],"The investigating officer concluded that neither the complainant nor the respondent had provided sufficient documentary evidence to support their respective claims and that he therefore recommended that the case be dismissed for lack of merit.","'Has provided' → 'had provided'; 'recommend' → 'recommended'; subjunctive 'be dismissed' stays; 'I' → 'he.'",["tense backshift","subjunctive","formal reporting"]))
ALL.append(q(425,"Hard",'Convert to indirect speech: "What specific measures will the agency implement to prevent a recurrence of the irregularities that were uncovered during the most recent audit?" the congressional oversight committee asked the agency head.',["The congressional oversight committee asked the agency head what specific measures the agency would implement to prevent a recurrence of the irregularities that had been uncovered during the most recent audit.","The congressional oversight committee asked the agency head what specific measures will the agency implement to prevent a recurrence of the irregularities.","The congressional oversight committee asked the agency head what specific measures would the agency implement to prevent a recurrence of the irregularities that had been uncovered during the most recent audit.","The congressional oversight committee asked the agency head that what specific measures the agency would implement to prevent a recurrence."],"The congressional oversight committee asked the agency head what specific measures the agency would implement to prevent a recurrence of the irregularities that had been uncovered during the most recent audit.","Wh-question: normal order; 'will implement' → 'would implement'; 'were uncovered' → 'had been uncovered.'",["wh-question","tense backshift","passive voice"]))
ALL.append(q(426,"Hard",'Convert to direct speech: The minister assured the public that the government had been working tirelessly to address the crisis and that significant progress had been made in the previous two weeks.',["The minister said, \"The government has been working tirelessly to address the crisis, and significant progress has been made in the last two weeks.\"","The minister said, \"The government had been working tirelessly to address the crisis, and significant progress had been made in the previous two weeks.\"","The minister said, \"The government is working tirelessly to address the crisis, and significant progress is being made in the last two weeks.\"","The minister said, \"We have been working tirelessly to address the crisis, and significant progress has been made in the last two weeks.\""],"The minister said, \"The government has been working tirelessly to address the crisis, and significant progress has been made in the last two weeks.\"","Reverse: 'had been working' → 'has been working'; 'had been made' → 'has been made'; 'the previous two weeks' → 'the last two weeks.'",["indirect to direct","reverse backshift","time expression"]))
ALL.append(q(427,"Hard",'Convert to direct speech: She asked him whether he had ever considered the possibility that the entire project might have been based on flawed assumptions from the very beginning.',["She asked him, \"Have you ever considered the possibility that the entire project might have been based on flawed assumptions from the very beginning?\"","She asked him, \"Had you ever considered the possibility that the entire project might have been based on flawed assumptions?\"","She asked him, \"Do you ever consider the possibility that the entire project might be based on flawed assumptions?\"","She asked him, \"Have you ever considered the possibility that the entire project may have been based on flawed assumptions from the very beginning?\""],"She asked him, \"Have you ever considered the possibility that the entire project might have been based on flawed assumptions from the very beginning?\"","Reverse: 'had considered' → 'have considered'; 'might have been' stays (already past modal); restore question form.",["indirect to direct","reverse backshift","yes/no question"]))
ALL.append(q(428,"Hard",'"I categorically deny all the allegations that have been made against me, and I demand that a thorough and impartial investigation be conducted to clear my name," the accused official said at the press conference.',["The accused official said at the press conference that he categorically denied all the allegations that had been made against him and that he demanded that a thorough and impartial investigation be conducted to clear his name.","The accused official said that he categorically denies all the allegations that have been made against him and demands that a thorough and impartial investigation be conducted.","The accused official said that he categorically denied all the allegations that had been made against him and demanded that a thorough and impartial investigation was conducted to clear his name.","The accused official said that I categorically deny all the allegations that have been made against me and demand that a thorough and impartial investigation be conducted."],"The accused official said at the press conference that he categorically denied all the allegations that had been made against him and that he demanded that a thorough and impartial investigation be conducted to clear his name.","'Deny' → 'denied'; 'have been made' → 'had been made'; 'demand' → 'demanded'; subjunctive 'be conducted' stays; 'I/me/my' → 'he/him/his.'",["tense backshift","subjunctive","pronoun change"]))
ALL.append(q(429,"Hard",'"I wish to place on record my strong objection to the manner in which this investigation has been conducted, as I believe that my constitutional rights have been violated at every stage of the proceedings," the respondent declared before the tribunal.',["The respondent declared before the tribunal that he wished to place on record his strong objection to the manner in which that investigation had been conducted, as he believed that his constitutional rights had been violated at every stage of the proceedings.","The respondent declared that he wishes to place on record his strong objection to the manner in which this investigation has been conducted.","The respondent declared that he wished to place on record his strong objection to the manner in which that investigation had been conducted, as he believed that his constitutional rights have been violated.","The respondent declared that I wish to place on record my strong objection to the manner in which this investigation has been conducted."],"The respondent declared before the tribunal that he wished to place on record his strong objection to the manner in which that investigation had been conducted, as he believed that his constitutional rights had been violated at every stage of the proceedings.","'Wish' → 'wished'; 'has been conducted' → 'had been conducted'; 'believe' → 'believed'; 'have been violated' → 'had been violated'; 'I/my' → 'he/his'; 'this' → 'that.'",["tense backshift","formal reporting","compound sentence"]))
ALL.append(q(430,"Hard",'"I am not in a position to comment on the ongoing investigation, but I can assure you that the agency is fully cooperating with all the relevant authorities and that we have nothing to hide," the spokesperson said.',["The spokesperson said that she was not in a position to comment on the ongoing investigation but that she could assure them that the agency was fully cooperating with all the relevant authorities and that they had nothing to hide.","The spokesperson said that she is not in a position to comment on the ongoing investigation but she can assure them that the agency is fully cooperating.","The spokesperson said that she was not in a position to comment on the ongoing investigation but that she could assure you that the agency was fully cooperating and that we had nothing to hide.","The spokesperson said that she was not in a position to comment on the ongoing investigation but she could assure them that the agency was fully cooperating and they have nothing to hide."],"The spokesperson said that she was not in a position to comment on the ongoing investigation but that she could assure them that the agency was fully cooperating with all the relevant authorities and that they had nothing to hide.","'Am not' → 'was not'; 'can' → 'could'; 'is cooperating' → 'was cooperating'; 'have' → 'had'; 'I' → 'she'; 'you' → 'them'; 'we' → 'they.'",["tense backshift","compound sentence","pronoun change"]))

ALL.append(q(431,"Hard",'Choose the CORRECT indirect speech for: "I shall not be moved by threats or intimidation, for I know that truth and justice are on my side," the whistleblower declared.',["The whistleblower declared that he would not be moved by threats or intimidation, for he knew that truth and justice were on his side.","The whistleblower declared that he shall not be moved by threats or intimidation, for he knows that truth and justice are on his side.","The whistleblower declared that he would not be moved by threats or intimidation, for he knew that truth and justice are on his side.","The whistleblower declared that I shall not be moved by threats or intimidation, for I know that truth and justice are on my side."],"The whistleblower declared that he would not be moved by threats or intimidation, for he knew that truth and justice were on his side.","'Shall not' → 'would not'; 'know' → 'knew'; 'are' → 'were'; 'I/my' → 'he/his.'",["tense backshift","modal verb","pronoun change"]))
ALL.append(q(432,"Hard",'Choose the CORRECT indirect speech for: "Had the proper procedures been followed from the outset, none of these problems would have arisen, and we would not be in this predicament today," the review panel concluded.',["The review panel concluded that had the proper procedures been followed from the outset, none of those problems would have arisen, and they would not have been in that predicament that day.","The review panel concluded that if the proper procedures had been followed from the outset, none of those problems would have arisen, and they would not be in that predicament.","The review panel concluded that had the proper procedures been followed from the outset, none of these problems would have arisen, and we would not be in this predicament today.","The review panel concluded that if the proper procedures had been followed from the outset, none of those problems would have arisen, and they would not have been in that predicament that day."],"The review panel concluded that if the proper procedures had been followed from the outset, none of those problems would have arisen, and they would not have been in that predicament that day.","Type 3 conditional stays; 'would not be' → 'would not have been' (aligning with past context); 'we' → 'they'; 'these' → 'those'; 'today' → 'that day.'",["conditional","pronoun change","time expression"]))
ALL.append(q(433,"Hard",'Choose the CORRECT indirect speech for: "I am of the firm opinion that the proposed legislation, if enacted in its current form, will do more harm than good to the very communities it purports to protect," the senator argued.',["The senator argued that he was of the firm opinion that the proposed legislation, if enacted in its current form, would do more harm than good to the very communities it purported to protect.","The senator argued that he is of the firm opinion that the proposed legislation, if enacted in its current form, will do more harm than good.","The senator argued that he was of the firm opinion that the proposed legislation, if enacted in its current form, will do more harm than good to the very communities it purports to protect.","The senator argued that I am of the firm opinion that the proposed legislation would do more harm than good."],"The senator argued that he was of the firm opinion that the proposed legislation, if enacted in its current form, would do more harm than good to the very communities it purported to protect.","'Am' → 'was'; 'will do' → 'would do'; 'purports' → 'purported'; 'I' → 'he.'",["tense backshift","embedded clause","formal reporting"]))
ALL.append(q(434,"Hard",'Choose the CORRECT indirect speech for: "Why has the government not yet released the funds that were appropriated by Congress six months ago for the rehabilitation of the typhoon-affected areas?" the opposition leader demanded.',["The opposition leader demanded to know why the government had not yet released the funds that had been appropriated by Congress six months before for the rehabilitation of the typhoon-affected areas.","The opposition leader demanded why has the government not yet released the funds that were appropriated by Congress six months ago.","The opposition leader demanded to know why the government has not yet released the funds that were appropriated by Congress six months ago.","The opposition leader demanded why the government had not yet released the funds that had been appropriated by Congress six months before."],"The opposition leader demanded to know why the government had not yet released the funds that had been appropriated by Congress six months before for the rehabilitation of the typhoon-affected areas.","'Has not released' → 'had not released'; 'were appropriated' → 'had been appropriated'; 'six months ago' → 'six months before.'",["wh-question","tense backshift","time expression"]))
ALL.append(q(435,"Hard",'Choose the CORRECT indirect speech for: "I promise you that I will leave no stone unturned in my pursuit of the truth, and I will not rest until every person responsible for this travesty has been brought to justice," the special prosecutor vowed.',["The special prosecutor vowed that he would leave no stone unturned in his pursuit of the truth and that he would not rest until every person responsible for that travesty had been brought to justice.","The special prosecutor vowed that he will leave no stone unturned in his pursuit of the truth and he will not rest until every person responsible has been brought to justice.","The special prosecutor vowed that he would leave no stone unturned in his pursuit of the truth and that he would not rest until every person responsible for that travesty has been brought to justice.","The special prosecutor vowed that I will leave no stone unturned in my pursuit of the truth and I will not rest until every person responsible has been brought to justice."],"The special prosecutor vowed that he would leave no stone unturned in his pursuit of the truth and that he would not rest until every person responsible for that travesty had been brought to justice.","'Will leave' → 'would leave'; 'will not rest' → 'would not rest'; 'has been brought' → 'had been brought'; 'I/my' → 'he/his'; 'this' → 'that.'",["tense backshift","compound sentence","pronoun change"]))
ALL.append(q(436,"Hard",'Which sentence contains an error in indirect speech?',["He told me that he had been waiting for over an hour.","She asked whether I could help her with the project.","The teacher said the students that they should study harder.","They informed us that the meeting had been postponed."],"The teacher said the students that they should study harder.","Error: 'said the students' is wrong. 'Said' cannot take a personal object directly. Should be 'told the students' or 'said to the students.'",["error recognition","reporting verb","grammar rule"]))
ALL.append(q(437,"Hard",'Which sentence contains an error in indirect speech?',["She asked me what time the train departed.","He told her that he would call her the next day.","The officer asked where was the nearest hospital.","They said that they had already finished the work."],"The officer asked where was the nearest hospital.","Error: Inverted word order. Should be 'where the nearest hospital was' (normal order in indirect questions).",["error recognition","word order","wh-question"]))
ALL.append(q(438,"Hard",'Which sentence contains an error in indirect speech?',["He said that he might be late for the meeting.","She told me that she had seen him the previous day.","The manager asked if did anyone have questions.","They announced that the event would be held the following week."],"The manager asked if did anyone have questions.","Error: 'if did anyone have' retains auxiliary 'did' and inverted order. Should be 'if anyone had any questions.'",["error recognition","word order","auxiliary removal"]))
ALL.append(q(439,"Hard",'Which sentence contains an error in indirect speech?',["She reminded me to bring my identification card.","He denied that he had taken the money.","The principal told the students to not run in the corridors.","They admitted that they had made a mistake."],"The principal told the students to not run in the corridors.","Error: Split infinitive 'to not run.' Correct form: 'not to run' (negative before 'to').",["error recognition","negative command","infinitive structure"]))
ALL.append(q(440,"Hard",'Which sentence contains an error in indirect speech?',["He asked me how much the book costed.","She said that she was feeling much better.","They told us that they would arrive by noon.","The doctor advised him to get more rest."],"He asked me how much the book costed.","Error: 'costed' is not the correct past tense of 'cost.' 'Cost' is irregular — past tense is also 'cost.'",["error recognition","irregular verb","tense backshift"]))

ALL.append(q(441,"Hard",'Choose the BEST conversion: "I have reason to believe that the documents that were presented to the court may have been falsified, and I intend to file a motion to have them examined by an independent forensic expert," the defense attorney said.',["The defense attorney said that he had reason to believe that the documents that had been presented to the court might have been falsified and that he intended to file a motion to have them examined by an independent forensic expert.","The defense attorney said that he has reason to believe that the documents that were presented to the court may have been falsified and he intends to file a motion.","The defense attorney said that he had reason to believe that the documents that had been presented to the court may have been falsified and that he intended to file a motion.","The defense attorney said that he had reason to believe that the documents that had been presented to the court might have been falsified and he intends to file a motion."],"The defense attorney said that he had reason to believe that the documents that had been presented to the court might have been falsified and that he intended to file a motion to have them examined by an independent forensic expert.","'Have reason' → 'had reason'; 'were presented' → 'had been presented'; 'may have been' → 'might have been'; 'intend' → 'intended'; 'I' → 'he.'",["tense backshift","modal verb","formal reporting"]))
ALL.append(q(442,"Hard",'Choose the BEST conversion: "I cannot in good conscience support a measure that I know will disproportionately affect the most vulnerable members of our society," the dissenting legislator said during the floor debate.',["The dissenting legislator said during the floor debate that she could not in good conscience support a measure that she knew would disproportionately affect the most vulnerable members of their society.","The dissenting legislator said that she cannot in good conscience support a measure that she knows will disproportionately affect the most vulnerable members of their society.","The dissenting legislator said that she could not in good conscience support a measure that she knew will disproportionately affect the most vulnerable members of our society.","The dissenting legislator said that I cannot in good conscience support a measure that I know will disproportionately affect the most vulnerable members of our society."],"The dissenting legislator said during the floor debate that she could not in good conscience support a measure that she knew would disproportionately affect the most vulnerable members of their society.","'Cannot' → 'could not'; 'know' → 'knew'; 'will affect' → 'would affect'; 'I' → 'she'; 'our' → 'their.'",["tense backshift","modal verb","pronoun change"]))
ALL.append(q(443,"Hard",'Choose the BEST conversion: "What assurance can you give us that the same mistakes will not be repeated in the future, given that similar promises were made three years ago and nothing has changed?" the citizens\' group asked the mayor.',["The citizens' group asked the mayor what assurance he could give them that the same mistakes would not be repeated in the future, given that similar promises had been made three years before and nothing had changed.","The citizens' group asked the mayor what assurance can he give them that the same mistakes will not be repeated in the future.","The citizens' group asked the mayor what assurance he could give them that the same mistakes would not be repeated in the future, given that similar promises were made three years ago and nothing has changed.","The citizens' group asked the mayor what assurance could he give them that the same mistakes would not be repeated."],"The citizens' group asked the mayor what assurance he could give them that the same mistakes would not be repeated in the future, given that similar promises had been made three years before and nothing had changed.","'Can give' → 'could give'; 'will not be' → 'would not be'; 'were made' → 'had been made'; 'has changed' → 'had changed'; 'you' → 'he'; 'us' → 'them'; 'three years ago' → 'three years before.'",["wh-question","tense backshift","time expression"]))
ALL.append(q(444,"Hard",'Choose the BEST conversion: "I hereby order the respondent to cease and desist from all activities that have been found to be in violation of the environmental protection laws, effective immediately," the judge ruled.',["The judge ruled that the respondent was ordered to cease and desist from all activities that had been found to be in violation of the environmental protection laws, effective immediately.","The judge ordered the respondent to cease and desist from all activities that had been found to be in violation of the environmental protection laws, effective immediately.","The judge ruled that he hereby orders the respondent to cease and desist from all activities that have been found to be in violation.","The judge ruled that I hereby order the respondent to cease and desist from all activities."],"The judge ordered the respondent to cease and desist from all activities that had been found to be in violation of the environmental protection laws, effective immediately.","Performative 'I hereby order' → simplified to 'ordered + person + to + verb'; 'have been found' → 'had been found.'",["reporting verb","infinitive structure","formal reporting"]))
ALL.append(q(445,"Hard",'Choose the BEST conversion: "I would like to express my sincere gratitude to everyone who has contributed to the success of this project, and I look forward to working with all of you on future endeavors," the project director said at the closing ceremony.',["The project director said at the closing ceremony that she would like to express her sincere gratitude to everyone who had contributed to the success of that project and that she looked forward to working with all of them on future endeavors.","The project director said that she would like to express her sincere gratitude to everyone who has contributed to the success of this project and she looks forward to working with all of you.","The project director said that she would like to express her sincere gratitude to everyone who had contributed to the success of that project and that she looked forward to working with all of you on future endeavors.","The project director said that she would liked to express her sincere gratitude to everyone who had contributed."],"The project director said at the closing ceremony that she would like to express her sincere gratitude to everyone who had contributed to the success of that project and that she looked forward to working with all of them on future endeavors.","'Would like' stays; 'has contributed' → 'had contributed'; 'look forward' → 'looked forward'; 'I/my' → 'she/her'; 'you' → 'them'; 'this' → 'that.'",["tense backshift","compound sentence","pronoun change"]))
ALL.append(q(446,"Hard",'In the sentence "The witness testified that the accused had entered the building at 9 PM," what was the original tense used by the witness?',["Simple past: \"The accused entered the building at 9 PM.\"","Past perfect: \"The accused had entered the building at 9 PM.\"","Present perfect: \"The accused has entered the building at 9 PM.\"","Simple present: \"The accused enters the building at 9 PM.\""],"Simple past: \"The accused entered the building at 9 PM.\"","In indirect speech, past perfect ('had entered') is the backshifted form of simple past ('entered').",["reverse backshift","tense identification","analysis"]))
ALL.append(q(447,"Hard",'In the sentence "She said that she was studying for the exam," what was the original tense?',["Present continuous: \"I am studying for the exam.\"","Past continuous: \"I was studying for the exam.\"","Present simple: \"I study for the exam.\"","Past perfect continuous: \"I had been studying for the exam.\""],"Present continuous: \"I am studying for the exam.\"","Past continuous ('was studying') is the backshifted form of present continuous ('am studying').",["reverse backshift","tense identification","analysis"]))
ALL.append(q(448,"Hard",'In the sentence "He asked if I could help him," what was the original question?',["\"Can you help me?\"","\"Could you help me?\"","\"Will you help me?\"","\"Would you help me?\""],"\"Can you help me?\"","'Could' in indirect speech is the backshifted form of 'can.' Reverse: 'could' → 'can'; 'I' → 'you'; 'him' → 'me.'",["reverse backshift","tense identification","yes/no question"]))
ALL.append(q(449,"Hard",'In the sentence "They told us that they would arrive the following day," what were the original words?',["\"We will arrive tomorrow.\"","\"We would arrive the following day.\"","\"They will arrive tomorrow.\"","\"We will arrive the next day.\""],"\"We will arrive tomorrow.\"","Reverse: 'would' → 'will'; 'they' → 'we'; 'the following day' → 'tomorrow.'",["reverse backshift","time expression","pronoun change"]))
ALL.append(q(450,"Hard",'In the sentence "She said that she had never been to Europe," what was the original statement?',["\"I have never been to Europe.\"","\"I had never been to Europe.\"","\"She has never been to Europe.\"","\"I never went to Europe.\""],"\"I have never been to Europe.\"","Past perfect ('had never been') is the backshifted form of present perfect ('have never been'). 'She' → 'I.'",["reverse backshift","tense identification","present perfect"]))

ALL.append(q(451,"Hard",'Choose the sentence where tense backshift is NOT required.',["The teacher said, \"The sun rises in the east.\"","He said, \"I am going to the store.\"","She said, \"I will call you tomorrow.\"","They said, \"We have finished the project.\""],"The teacher said, \"The sun rises in the east.\"","Universal truths/scientific facts do not require tense backshift even when the reporting verb is past.",["no tense change","universal truth","analysis"]))
ALL.append(q(452,"Hard",'Choose the sentence where tense backshift is NOT required.',["She said, \"I could swim when I was young.\"","He said, \"I am tired.\"","They said, \"We will come tomorrow.\"","She said, \"I have a headache.\""],"She said, \"I could swim when I was young.\"","'Could' is already a past modal and does not backshift further.",["no tense change","modal verb","analysis"]))
ALL.append(q(453,"Hard",'Choose the sentence where tense backshift is NOT required.',["He said, \"If I were rich, I would travel the world.\"","She said, \"I like chocolate.\"","They said, \"We are leaving now.\"","He said, \"I will help you.\""],"He said, \"If I were rich, I would travel the world.\"","Type 2 conditionals (unreal present) use 'were' and 'would' which do not backshift.",["no tense change","conditional","analysis"]))
ALL.append(q(454,"Hard",'Choose the sentence where tense backshift is NOT required.',["He says, \"I am happy.\"","He said, \"I am happy.\"","He said, \"I was happy.\"","He said, \"I have been happy.\""],"He says, \"I am happy.\"","When the reporting verb is present tense ('says'), no backshift is needed.",["no tense change","present reporting verb","analysis"]))
ALL.append(q(455,"Hard",'Choose the sentence where tense backshift is NOT required.',["She said, \"I should have studied harder.\"","She said, \"I study every day.\"","She said, \"I am studying now.\"","She said, \"I will study tomorrow.\""],"She said, \"I should have studied harder.\"","'Should have' is a past modal perfect and does not backshift further.",["no tense change","modal verb","analysis"]))
ALL.append(q(456,"Hard",'A government memo states: "All department heads are hereby directed to submit their quarterly reports not later than the 15th of the following month." Convert to indirect speech.',["The memo directed all department heads to submit their quarterly reports not later than the 15th of the following month.","The memo said that all department heads are hereby directed to submit their quarterly reports.","The memo stated that all department heads were hereby directed to submit their quarterly reports not later than the 15th of the following month.","The memo directed that all department heads should submitted their quarterly reports."],"The memo directed all department heads to submit their quarterly reports not later than the 15th of the following month.","Official directives are best reported using: directed + person + to + verb (infinitive structure).",["formal reporting","infinitive structure","reporting verb"]))
ALL.append(q(457,"Hard",'A notice reads: "Applicants who fail to submit complete requirements within the prescribed period shall be deemed to have waived their right to the position." Convert to indirect speech.',["The notice stated that applicants who failed to submit complete requirements within the prescribed period would be deemed to have waived their right to the position.","The notice stated that applicants who fail to submit complete requirements within the prescribed period shall be deemed to have waived their right.","The notice stated that applicants who failed to submit complete requirements within the prescribed period shall be deemed to have waived their right to the position.","The notice said that applicants who had failed to submit complete requirements would be deemed to have waived their right."],"The notice stated that applicants who failed to submit complete requirements within the prescribed period would be deemed to have waived their right to the position.","'Fail' → 'failed'; 'shall be deemed' → 'would be deemed.'",["tense backshift","formal reporting","passive voice"]))
ALL.append(q(458,"Hard",'Choose the correct indirect form for this multi-speaker dialogue: Maria said, "I told Juan yesterday that I would help him, but he said he didn\'t need my help."',["Maria said that she had told Juan the previous day that she would help him, but he had said he hadn't needed her help.","Maria said that she told Juan yesterday that she would help him, but he said he didn't need her help.","Maria said that she had told Juan the previous day that she would help him, but he had said he didn't need her help.","Maria said that I told Juan yesterday that I would help him, but he said he didn't need my help."],"Maria said that she had told Juan the previous day that she would help him, but he had said he hadn't needed her help.","'Told' → 'had told'; 'said' → 'had said'; 'didn't need' → 'hadn't needed'; 'I/my' → 'she/her'; 'yesterday' → 'the previous day.'",["tense backshift","compound sentence","time expression"]))
ALL.append(q(459,"Hard",'Choose the correct indirect form: The sign at the entrance read, "No unauthorized personnel beyond this point. Violators will be prosecuted."',["The sign at the entrance stated that no unauthorized personnel were allowed beyond that point and that violators would be prosecuted.","The sign at the entrance read that no unauthorized personnel beyond this point and violators will be prosecuted.","The sign at the entrance stated that no unauthorized personnel are allowed beyond that point and violators will be prosecuted.","The sign at the entrance said that no unauthorized personnel beyond this point and that violators would be prosecuted."],"The sign at the entrance stated that no unauthorized personnel were allowed beyond that point and that violators would be prosecuted.","Signs/notices: 'stated that'; implied 'are allowed' → 'were allowed'; 'will be' → 'would be'; 'this' → 'that.'",["formal reporting","tense backshift","place expression"]))
ALL.append(q(460,"Hard",'Choose the correct indirect form for this complex question: "Given that the previous administration had already approved the project and allocated funds for its implementation, why is the current administration now claiming that the project is not feasible?" the opposition senator asked.',["The opposition senator asked why the current administration was then claiming that the project was not feasible, given that the previous administration had already approved the project and allocated funds for its implementation.","The opposition senator asked why is the current administration now claiming that the project is not feasible, given that the previous administration had already approved the project.","The opposition senator asked why the current administration was now claiming that the project was not feasible, given that the previous administration had already approved the project and allocated funds for its implementation.","The opposition senator asked that why the current administration was claiming that the project was not feasible."],"The opposition senator asked why the current administration was then claiming that the project was not feasible, given that the previous administration had already approved the project and allocated funds for its implementation.","'Is claiming' → 'was claiming'; 'is not' → 'was not'; past perfect stays; 'now' → 'then.'",["wh-question","tense backshift","time expression"]))

ALL.append(q(461,"Hard",'Choose the correct form: "I have been reliably informed that certain individuals within this organization have been systematically undermining the reforms that we have worked so hard to implement," the reformist director alleged.',["The reformist director alleged that she had been reliably informed that certain individuals within that organization had been systematically undermining the reforms that they had worked so hard to implement.","The reformist director alleged that she has been reliably informed that certain individuals within this organization have been systematically undermining the reforms.","The reformist director alleged that she had been reliably informed that certain individuals within that organization had been systematically undermining the reforms that they have worked so hard to implement.","The reformist director alleged that I had been reliably informed that certain individuals within this organization had been systematically undermining the reforms."],"The reformist director alleged that she had been reliably informed that certain individuals within that organization had been systematically undermining the reforms that they had worked so hard to implement.","All present perfects → past perfects; 'I' → 'she'; 'we' → 'they'; 'this' → 'that.'",["tense backshift","compound sentence","pronoun change"]))
ALL.append(q(462,"Hard",'Choose the correct form: "Let me make one thing perfectly clear: I will not resign, I have done nothing wrong, and I will fight these baseless accusations with every legal means at my disposal," the embattled official declared.',["The embattled official declared that he would not resign, that he had done nothing wrong, and that he would fight those baseless accusations with every legal means at his disposal.","The embattled official declared that he will not resign, he has done nothing wrong, and he will fight these baseless accusations.","The embattled official declared that he would not resign, he had done nothing wrong, and he would fight those baseless accusations with every legal means at my disposal.","The embattled official declared that I will not resign, I have done nothing wrong, and I will fight these baseless accusations."],"The embattled official declared that he would not resign, that he had done nothing wrong, and that he would fight those baseless accusations with every legal means at his disposal.","'Will not resign' → 'would not resign'; 'have done' → 'had done'; 'will fight' → 'would fight'; 'I/my' → 'he/his'; 'these' → 'those.'",["tense backshift","compound sentence","pronoun change"]))
ALL.append(q(463,"Hard",'Choose the correct form: "I wonder whether the people who are criticizing us now would have done any better had they been in our position," the outgoing secretary mused.',["The outgoing secretary mused whether the people who were criticizing them then would have done any better had they been in their position.","The outgoing secretary mused whether the people who are criticizing them now would have done any better had they been in their position.","The outgoing secretary mused that she wondered whether the people who were criticizing them then would have done any better had they been in their position.","The outgoing secretary mused whether the people who were criticizing us now would have done any better had they been in our position."],"The outgoing secretary mused whether the people who were criticizing them then would have done any better had they been in their position.","'Are criticizing' → 'were criticizing'; 'us' → 'them'; 'our' → 'their'; 'now' → 'then'; conditional stays.",["tense backshift","conditional","pronoun change"]))
ALL.append(q(464,"Hard",'Choose the correct form: "I respectfully submit that the evidence presented by the prosecution is circumstantial at best and does not meet the threshold of proof beyond reasonable doubt that is required for a conviction," the defense counsel argued before the court.',["The defense counsel argued before the court that the evidence presented by the prosecution was circumstantial at best and did not meet the threshold of proof beyond reasonable doubt that was required for a conviction.","The defense counsel argued that the evidence presented by the prosecution is circumstantial at best and does not meet the threshold of proof beyond reasonable doubt.","The defense counsel argued that the evidence presented by the prosecution was circumstantial at best and does not meet the threshold of proof beyond reasonable doubt that was required for a conviction.","The defense counsel argued that I respectfully submit that the evidence presented by the prosecution is circumstantial at best."],"The defense counsel argued before the court that the evidence presented by the prosecution was circumstantial at best and did not meet the threshold of proof beyond reasonable doubt that was required for a conviction.","'Is circumstantial' → 'was circumstantial'; 'does not meet' → 'did not meet'; 'is required' → 'was required.' Simplified from 'I respectfully submit.'",["tense backshift","formal reporting","embedded clause"]))
ALL.append(q(465,"Hard",'Choose the correct form: "I am pleased to announce that, after months of negotiations, we have finally reached an agreement with the labor union that will benefit both the employees and the organization," the HR director said.',["The HR director said that she was pleased to announce that, after months of negotiations, they had finally reached an agreement with the labor union that would benefit both the employees and the organization.","The HR director said that she is pleased to announce that they have finally reached an agreement with the labor union that will benefit both the employees and the organization.","The HR director said that she was pleased to announce that, after months of negotiations, they had finally reached an agreement with the labor union that will benefit both the employees and the organization.","The HR director said that I am pleased to announce that we have finally reached an agreement."],"The HR director said that she was pleased to announce that, after months of negotiations, they had finally reached an agreement with the labor union that would benefit both the employees and the organization.","'Am pleased' → 'was pleased'; 'have reached' → 'had reached'; 'will benefit' → 'would benefit'; 'I' → 'she'; 'we' → 'they.'",["tense backshift","compound sentence","pronoun change"]))
ALL.append(q(466,"Hard",'Choose the BEST answer. Which reporting verb pattern is INCORRECT?',["He suggested that we leave early.","She admitted having made a mistake.","He denied to take the money.","They insisted that the meeting be postponed."],"He denied to take the money.","'Deny' takes a gerund (-ing), not an infinitive. Correct: 'denied taking the money.'",["error recognition","reporting verb","gerund"]))
ALL.append(q(467,"Hard",'Choose the BEST answer. Which reporting verb pattern is INCORRECT?',["She recommended that he apply for the position.","He accused me of cheating on the exam.","She suggested me to try a different approach.","They congratulated her on winning the award."],"She suggested me to try a different approach.","'Suggest' does not take object + infinitive. Correct: 'suggested that I try' or 'suggested trying.'",["error recognition","reporting verb","grammar rule"]))
ALL.append(q(468,"Hard",'Choose the BEST answer. Which reporting verb pattern is INCORRECT?',["He apologized for being late.","She blamed him for the failure.","He explained me the situation.","They warned us not to go there."],"He explained me the situation.","'Explain' does not take an indirect object directly. Correct: 'explained the situation to me.'",["error recognition","reporting verb","grammar rule"]))
ALL.append(q(469,"Hard",'Choose the BEST answer. Which sentence correctly uses "whether" in indirect speech?',["She asked whether I was coming or not.","She asked whether was I coming.","She asked whether that I was coming.","She asked whether I was coming or no."],"She asked whether I was coming or not.","'Whether' + normal word order + optional 'or not' is the correct pattern.",["conjunction","yes/no question","grammar rule"]))
ALL.append(q(470,"Hard",'Choose the BEST answer. In which sentence is the use of "that" OPTIONAL?',["He said that he was tired.","She asked that I was ready.","He told that he was leaving.","She suggested that we leave."],"He said that he was tired.","After 'said,' 'that' is optional: 'He said he was tired' is also correct. In the other options, 'that' is either wrong or required.",["conjunction","grammar rule","usage"]))

ALL.append(q(471,"Hard",'Choose the correct indirect speech for this CSE-style item: The Civil Service Commission announced, "All examinees must bring two valid IDs and their notice of admission to the testing center on the day of the examination."',["The Civil Service Commission announced that all examinees had to bring two valid IDs and their notice of admission to the testing center on the day of the examination.","The Civil Service Commission announced that all examinees must bring two valid IDs and their notice of admission to the testing center on the day of the examination.","The Civil Service Commission announced all examinees to bring two valid IDs and their notice of admission.","The Civil Service Commission announced that all examinees must brought two valid IDs and their notice of admission."],"The Civil Service Commission announced that all examinees had to bring two valid IDs and their notice of admission to the testing center on the day of the examination.","'Must' (obligation) → 'had to' when reporting verb is past.",["tense backshift","modal verb","formal reporting"]))
ALL.append(q(472,"Hard",'Choose the correct indirect speech: "I strongly object to the characterization of my actions as negligent, and I maintain that I acted in full compliance with all applicable regulations and guidelines," the respondent stated in his counter-affidavit.',["The respondent stated in his counter-affidavit that he strongly objected to the characterization of his actions as negligent and that he maintained that he had acted in full compliance with all applicable regulations and guidelines.","The respondent stated that he strongly objects to the characterization of his actions as negligent and maintains that he acted in full compliance.","The respondent stated that he strongly objected to the characterization of his actions as negligent and that he maintained that he acted in full compliance with all applicable regulations and guidelines.","The respondent stated that I strongly object to the characterization of my actions as negligent and I maintain that I acted in full compliance."],"The respondent stated in his counter-affidavit that he strongly objected to the characterization of his actions as negligent and that he maintained that he had acted in full compliance with all applicable regulations and guidelines.","'Object' → 'objected'; 'maintain' → 'maintained'; 'acted' → 'had acted'; 'I/my' → 'he/his.'",["tense backshift","formal reporting","compound sentence"]))
ALL.append(q(473,"Hard",'Choose the correct indirect speech: "What specific steps has your office taken to ensure that the irregularities identified in the COA report will not recur in the next fiscal year?" the committee chair asked the agency head.',["The committee chair asked the agency head what specific steps his office had taken to ensure that the irregularities identified in the COA report would not recur in the next fiscal year.","The committee chair asked the agency head what specific steps has his office taken to ensure that the irregularities will not recur.","The committee chair asked the agency head what specific steps had his office taken to ensure that the irregularities identified in the COA report would not recur.","The committee chair asked the agency head that what specific steps his office had taken to ensure that the irregularities would not recur."],"The committee chair asked the agency head what specific steps his office had taken to ensure that the irregularities identified in the COA report would not recur in the next fiscal year.","'Has taken' → 'had taken'; 'will not recur' → 'would not recur'; 'your' → 'his.' Normal word order.",["wh-question","tense backshift","formal reporting"]))
ALL.append(q(474,"Hard",'Choose the correct indirect speech: "I am confident that, with the cooperation of all stakeholders, we can overcome the challenges that lie ahead and build a more transparent and accountable government," the newly appointed secretary said in her inaugural address.',["The newly appointed secretary said in her inaugural address that she was confident that, with the cooperation of all stakeholders, they could overcome the challenges that lay ahead and build a more transparent and accountable government.","The newly appointed secretary said that she is confident that, with the cooperation of all stakeholders, they can overcome the challenges that lie ahead.","The newly appointed secretary said that she was confident that, with the cooperation of all stakeholders, they could overcome the challenges that lie ahead and build a more transparent and accountable government.","The newly appointed secretary said that I am confident that, with the cooperation of all stakeholders, we can overcome the challenges."],"The newly appointed secretary said in her inaugural address that she was confident that, with the cooperation of all stakeholders, they could overcome the challenges that lay ahead and build a more transparent and accountable government.","'Am confident' → 'was confident'; 'can overcome' → 'could overcome'; 'lie' → 'lay'; 'I' → 'she'; 'we' → 'they.'",["tense backshift","modal verb","pronoun change"]))
ALL.append(q(475,"Hard",'Choose the correct indirect speech: "I would have resigned long ago if I did not believe that my continued service could still make a meaningful difference in the lives of ordinary Filipinos," the embattled official said.',["The embattled official said that he would have resigned long before if he had not believed that his continued service could still make a meaningful difference in the lives of ordinary Filipinos.","The embattled official said that he would have resigned long ago if he did not believe that his continued service could still make a meaningful difference.","The embattled official said that he would resigned long ago if he did not believe that his continued service could still make a meaningful difference.","The embattled official said that I would have resigned long ago if I did not believe that my continued service could still make a meaningful difference."],"The embattled official said that he would have resigned long before if he had not believed that his continued service could still make a meaningful difference in the lives of ordinary Filipinos.","Mixed conditional: 'would have resigned' stays; 'did not believe' → 'had not believed'; 'ago' → 'before'; 'I/my' → 'he/his.'",["conditional","tense backshift","time expression"]))
ALL.append(q(476,"Hard",'CSE-style item: The memorandum stated, "All personnel are required to undergo the mandatory drug testing within thirty days from the date of this circular." Choose the correct indirect form.',["The memorandum stated that all personnel were required to undergo the mandatory drug testing within thirty days from the date of that circular.","The memorandum stated that all personnel are required to undergo the mandatory drug testing within thirty days from the date of this circular.","The memorandum stated that all personnel had been required to undergo the mandatory drug testing within thirty days.","The memorandum stated all personnel to undergo the mandatory drug testing within thirty days."],"The memorandum stated that all personnel were required to undergo the mandatory drug testing within thirty days from the date of that circular.","'Are required' → 'were required'; 'this' → 'that.'",["tense backshift","formal reporting","place expression"]))
ALL.append(q(477,"Hard",'CSE-style item: "I categorically state that at no time during my tenure as department head did I authorize, condone, or participate in any transaction that was not in accordance with established procurement procedures," the official declared under oath.',["The official declared under oath that he categorically stated that at no time during his tenure as department head had he authorized, condoned, or participated in any transaction that had not been in accordance with established procurement procedures.","The official declared under oath that at no time during his tenure as department head had he authorized, condoned, or participated in any transaction that was not in accordance with established procurement procedures.","The official declared under oath that he categorically states that at no time during his tenure did he authorize, condone, or participate in any transaction.","The official declared under oath that I categorically state that at no time during my tenure did I authorize any transaction."],"The official declared under oath that at no time during his tenure as department head had he authorized, condoned, or participated in any transaction that was not in accordance with established procurement procedures.","Simplified: 'did authorize' → 'had authorized'; 'I/my' → 'he/his.' 'Was not' can stay as past since past perfect is also acceptable.",["tense backshift","formal reporting","negative statement"]))
ALL.append(q(478,"Hard",'CSE-style item: Choose the sentence that is INCORRECTLY converted to indirect speech.',["The president said that the Philippines is committed to upholding human rights.","She asked me what time the meeting would start.","He told me that he has been waiting for two hours.","The teacher reminded the students not to forget their homework."],"He told me that he has been waiting for two hours.","Error: With past reporting verb 'told,' present perfect 'has been waiting' should backshift to 'had been waiting.'",["error recognition","tense backshift","present perfect"]))
ALL.append(q(479,"Hard",'CSE-style item: Choose the sentence that is INCORRECTLY converted to indirect speech.',["She said that she would come the following day.","He asked me where I had put his keys.","The officer told us to not park in the restricted area.","They announced that the event had been postponed."],"The officer told us to not park in the restricted area.","Error: Split infinitive. Correct: 'told us not to park' (negative before 'to').",["error recognition","negative command","infinitive structure"]))
ALL.append(q(480,"Hard",'CSE-style item: Choose the sentence that is INCORRECTLY converted to indirect speech.',["She wondered whether she should accept the offer.","He explained that the delay had been caused by the typhoon.","The manager asked why did the employee leave early.","They promised that they would complete the project on time."],"The manager asked why did the employee leave early.","Error: Retains inverted order with 'did.' Correct: 'asked why the employee had left early.'",["error recognition","word order","auxiliary removal"]))

ALL.append(q(481,"Hard",'CSE-style item: Choose the sentence that is CORRECTLY converted to indirect speech.',["He asked me that where I was going.","She told that she was not feeling well.","The director informed the staff that the office would be closed the following day.","He said me that he would be late."],"The director informed the staff that the office would be closed the following day.","Correct pattern: informed + person + that + clause. The others have errors: 'asked that where' (wrong conjunction), 'told that' (missing object), 'said me' (wrong verb).",["error recognition","reporting verb","grammar rule"]))
ALL.append(q(482,"Hard",'CSE-style item: Choose the sentence that is CORRECTLY converted to indirect speech.',["She asked if could I lend her some money.","He told me not to worry about the results.","The teacher said the students to open their books.","She asked that I was ready for the exam."],"He told me not to worry about the results.","Correct: told + person + not to + verb. Others have errors: inverted order, 'said + object,' 'asked that' for yes/no question.",["error recognition","negative command","grammar rule"]))
ALL.append(q(483,"Hard",'CSE-style item: Choose the sentence that is CORRECTLY converted to indirect speech.',["He asked where was the nearest ATM.","She said that she has already eaten.","The officer warned the driver not to exceed the speed limit.","They told that they would arrive by noon."],"The officer warned the driver not to exceed the speed limit.","Correct: warned + person + not to + verb. Others: inverted order, wrong tense (has → had), missing object after 'told.'",["error recognition","reporting verb","grammar rule"]))
ALL.append(q(484,"Hard",'CSE-style item: Choose the sentence that is CORRECTLY converted to indirect speech.',["She asked me how much did the ticket cost.","He denied that he had been involved in the incident.","The teacher told to the students to be quiet.","She said me that she would call later."],"He denied that he had been involved in the incident.","Correct: denied + that + clause. Others: retained 'did,' 'told to' (wrong preposition), 'said me' (wrong verb).",["error recognition","reporting verb","grammar rule"]))
ALL.append(q(485,"Hard",'CSE-style item: Choose the sentence that is CORRECTLY converted to indirect speech.',["He asked whether I had received his email.","She told that the meeting was cancelled.","The boss said his employees to work harder.","He asked that if I could help him."],"He asked whether I had received his email.","Correct: asked + whether + normal order + backshifted tense. Others: missing object, wrong verb pattern, redundant 'that if.'",["error recognition","yes/no question","grammar rule"]))
ALL.append(q(486,"Hard",'CSE-style comprehensive item: "I am writing to formally notify you that your application for promotion has been denied on the grounds that you have not met the minimum service requirement of three years, as stipulated in CSC Memorandum Circular No. 14, Series of 2023," the HR director wrote.',["The HR director wrote that she was formally notifying the recipient that his/her application for promotion had been denied on the grounds that he/she had not met the minimum service requirement of three years, as stipulated in CSC Memorandum Circular No. 14, Series of 2023.","The HR director wrote that she is writing to formally notify the recipient that the application for promotion has been denied.","The HR director wrote that I am writing to formally notify you that your application for promotion has been denied.","The HR director wrote that she was formally notifying the recipient that his/her application for promotion has been denied on the grounds that he/she has not met the minimum service requirement."],"The HR director wrote that she was formally notifying the recipient that his/her application for promotion had been denied on the grounds that he/she had not met the minimum service requirement of three years, as stipulated in CSC Memorandum Circular No. 14, Series of 2023.","'Am writing/notify' → 'was notifying'; 'has been denied' → 'had been denied'; 'have not met' → 'had not met'; 'I' → 'she'; 'you/your' → 'recipient/his/her.'",["tense backshift","formal reporting","compound sentence"]))
ALL.append(q(487,"Hard",'CSE-style comprehensive item: "I respectfully request that the Honorable Commission reconsider its resolution dated March 15, 2024, which I believe was issued without affording me the opportunity to present my side, in violation of my right to due process," the petitioner pleaded.',["The petitioner pleaded that the Honorable Commission reconsider its resolution dated March 15, 2024, which he believed had been issued without affording him the opportunity to present his side, in violation of his right to due process.","The petitioner pleaded that the Honorable Commission reconsidered its resolution dated March 15, 2024, which he believed was issued without affording him the opportunity.","The petitioner pleaded that I respectfully request that the Honorable Commission reconsider its resolution.","The petitioner pleaded that the Honorable Commission should reconsider its resolution dated March 15, 2024, which he believed had been issued without affording him the opportunity to present his side."],"The petitioner pleaded that the Honorable Commission reconsider its resolution dated March 15, 2024, which he believed had been issued without affording him the opportunity to present his side, in violation of his right to due process.","'Request that + subjunctive' stays; 'believe' → 'believed'; 'was issued' → 'had been issued'; 'I/me/my' → 'he/him/his.'",["subjunctive","tense backshift","formal reporting"]))
ALL.append(q(488,"Hard",'CSE-style comprehensive item: "Not only has the respondent failed to comply with the lawful order of this Commission, but he has also shown a pattern of deliberate defiance that cannot and should not be tolerated in a democratic society governed by the rule of law," the commissioner said in his resolution.',["The commissioner said in his resolution that not only had the respondent failed to comply with the lawful order of that Commission, but he had also shown a pattern of deliberate defiance that could not and should not be tolerated in a democratic society governed by the rule of law.","The commissioner said that not only has the respondent failed to comply with the lawful order of this Commission, but he has also shown a pattern of deliberate defiance.","The commissioner said that not only had the respondent failed to comply with the lawful order of that Commission, but he had also shown a pattern of deliberate defiance that cannot and should not be tolerated.","The commissioner said that not only had the respondent failed to comply, but he also showed a pattern of deliberate defiance that could not be tolerated."],"The commissioner said in his resolution that not only had the respondent failed to comply with the lawful order of that Commission, but he had also shown a pattern of deliberate defiance that could not and should not be tolerated in a democratic society governed by the rule of law.","'Has failed' → 'had failed'; 'has shown' → 'had shown'; 'cannot' → 'could not'; 'should not' stays; 'this' → 'that.'",["tense backshift","modal verb","formal reporting"]))
ALL.append(q(489,"Hard",'CSE-style item: Choose the BEST way to report this in a government memorandum: The Secretary said, "I direct all bureau directors to submit their respective action plans within fifteen days from receipt of this memorandum."',["The Secretary directed all bureau directors to submit their respective action plans within fifteen days from receipt of that memorandum.","The Secretary said that he directs all bureau directors to submit their respective action plans within fifteen days from receipt of this memorandum.","The Secretary said that all bureau directors are directed to submit their respective action plans within fifteen days.","The Secretary told all bureau directors that they should submitted their respective action plans within fifteen days."],"The Secretary directed all bureau directors to submit their respective action plans within fifteen days from receipt of that memorandum.","Official directives: simplified to 'directed + person + to + verb'; 'this' → 'that.'",["formal reporting","infinitive structure","reporting verb"]))
ALL.append(q(490,"Hard",'CSE-style item: Choose the BEST way to report: The resolution states, "Any employee found guilty of grave misconduct shall be dismissed from the service with forfeiture of all benefits."',["The resolution states that any employee found guilty of grave misconduct shall be dismissed from the service with forfeiture of all benefits.","The resolution stated that any employee found guilty of grave misconduct would be dismissed from the service with forfeiture of all benefits.","The resolution states that any employee found guilty of grave misconduct will be dismissed from the service with forfeiture of all benefits.","The resolution stated that any employee found guilty of grave misconduct shall be dismissed from the service."],"The resolution states that any employee found guilty of grave misconduct shall be dismissed from the service with forfeiture of all benefits.","When reporting a still-active legal document using present tense 'states,' no backshift is needed. 'Shall' stays in legal context.",["no tense change","formal reporting","present reporting verb"]))

ALL.append(q(491,"Hard",'CSE-style item: "I am submitting my irrevocable resignation effective immediately, as I can no longer in good conscience continue to serve in an administration that has repeatedly demonstrated its disregard for the welfare of the Filipino people," the undersecretary wrote.',["The undersecretary wrote that she was submitting her irrevocable resignation effective immediately, as she could no longer in good conscience continue to serve in an administration that had repeatedly demonstrated its disregard for the welfare of the Filipino people.","The undersecretary wrote that she is submitting her irrevocable resignation effective immediately, as she can no longer continue to serve.","The undersecretary wrote that she was submitting her irrevocable resignation effective immediately, as she could no longer continue to serve in an administration that has repeatedly demonstrated its disregard.","The undersecretary wrote that I am submitting my irrevocable resignation effective immediately."],"The undersecretary wrote that she was submitting her irrevocable resignation effective immediately, as she could no longer in good conscience continue to serve in an administration that had repeatedly demonstrated its disregard for the welfare of the Filipino people.","'Am submitting' → 'was submitting'; 'can' → 'could'; 'has demonstrated' → 'had demonstrated'; 'I/my' → 'she/her.'",["tense backshift","modal verb","formal reporting"]))
ALL.append(q(492,"Hard",'CSE-style item: "I move that the committee adopt the proposed amendments to the rules of procedure, which I believe will significantly improve the efficiency and transparency of our deliberations," the vice chairperson said.',["The vice chairperson moved that the committee adopt the proposed amendments to the rules of procedure, which she believed would significantly improve the efficiency and transparency of their deliberations.","The vice chairperson said that she moves that the committee adopt the proposed amendments to the rules of procedure.","The vice chairperson moved that the committee adopted the proposed amendments to the rules of procedure, which she believed would significantly improve the efficiency.","The vice chairperson said that I move that the committee adopt the proposed amendments."],"The vice chairperson moved that the committee adopt the proposed amendments to the rules of procedure, which she believed would significantly improve the efficiency and transparency of their deliberations.","'Move that' + subjunctive 'adopt' stays; 'believe' → 'believed'; 'will improve' → 'would improve'; 'I' → 'she'; 'our' → 'their.'",["subjunctive","tense backshift","formal reporting"]))
ALL.append(q(493,"Hard",'CSE-style item: Choose the INCORRECTLY reported sentence.',["The witness stated that he had seen the suspect flee the scene at approximately 10 PM.","The judge asked the defense counsel whether his client wished to change his plea.","The prosecutor argued that the evidence clearly showed that the accused was guilty.","The accused told the court that he is innocent and that he demands a fair trial."],"The accused told the court that he is innocent and that he demands a fair trial.","Error: Past reporting verb 'told' requires backshift: 'is' → 'was'; 'demands' → 'demanded.'",["error recognition","tense backshift","formal reporting"]))
ALL.append(q(494,"Hard",'CSE-style item: Choose the INCORRECTLY reported sentence.',["She explained that she had been unable to attend because her child had been sick.","He mentioned that he might apply for the position if it was still available.","The director announced that the office will be closed the following Monday for renovation.","They confirmed that they had received all the necessary documents."],"The director announced that the office will be closed the following Monday for renovation.","Error: Past reporting verb 'announced' requires: 'will be' → 'would be.'",["error recognition","tense backshift","modal verb"]))
ALL.append(q(495,"Hard",'CSE-style item: Choose the INCORRECTLY reported sentence.',["The teacher reminded the students that the deadline for submission was the following Friday.","He asked me politely if I could lend him my notes.","She complained that nobody listens to her suggestions.","The committee announced that the results had been released."],"She complained that nobody listens to her suggestions.","Error: Past reporting verb 'complained' requires: 'listens' → 'listened.'",["error recognition","tense backshift","present tense"]))
ALL.append(q(496,"Hard",'CSE-style comprehensive: "I have thoroughly reviewed the records and I am now fully convinced that the allegations against the respondent are without merit; accordingly, I recommend that the complaint be dismissed," the investigating officer concluded in her report.',["The investigating officer concluded in her report that she had thoroughly reviewed the records and was then fully convinced that the allegations against the respondent were without merit; accordingly, she recommended that the complaint be dismissed.","The investigating officer concluded that she has thoroughly reviewed the records and is now fully convinced that the allegations are without merit.","The investigating officer concluded that she had thoroughly reviewed the records and was fully convinced that the allegations against the respondent were without merit; accordingly, she recommended that the complaint was dismissed.","The investigating officer concluded that I have thoroughly reviewed the records and I am now fully convinced that the allegations are without merit."],"The investigating officer concluded in her report that she had thoroughly reviewed the records and was then fully convinced that the allegations against the respondent were without merit; accordingly, she recommended that the complaint be dismissed.","'Have reviewed' → 'had reviewed'; 'am convinced' → 'was convinced'; 'are' → 'were'; 'recommend' → 'recommended'; subjunctive 'be dismissed' stays; 'I' → 'she'; 'now' → 'then.'",["tense backshift","subjunctive","formal reporting"]))
ALL.append(q(497,"Hard",'CSE-style comprehensive: "I wish to inform the Honorable Court that my client has decided to withdraw his appeal, as he has accepted the decision of the lower court and wishes to begin serving his sentence immediately," the defense attorney said.',["The defense attorney said that he wished to inform the Honorable Court that his client had decided to withdraw his appeal, as he had accepted the decision of the lower court and wished to begin serving his sentence immediately.","The defense attorney said that he wishes to inform the Honorable Court that his client has decided to withdraw his appeal.","The defense attorney said that he wished to inform the Honorable Court that his client had decided to withdraw his appeal, as he has accepted the decision of the lower court.","The defense attorney said that I wish to inform the Honorable Court that my client has decided to withdraw his appeal."],"The defense attorney said that he wished to inform the Honorable Court that his client had decided to withdraw his appeal, as he had accepted the decision of the lower court and wished to begin serving his sentence immediately.","'Wish' → 'wished'; 'has decided' → 'had decided'; 'has accepted' → 'had accepted'; 'wishes' → 'wished'; 'I/my' → 'he/his.'",["tense backshift","formal reporting","compound sentence"]))
ALL.append(q(498,"Hard",'CSE-style comprehensive: "I cannot overemphasize the importance of maintaining the highest standards of integrity in public service, for it is only through the collective commitment of every government employee that we can hope to restore the people\'s trust in our institutions," the chairperson said in her keynote address.',["The chairperson said in her keynote address that she could not overemphasize the importance of maintaining the highest standards of integrity in public service, for it was only through the collective commitment of every government employee that they could hope to restore the people's trust in their institutions.","The chairperson said that she cannot overemphasize the importance of maintaining the highest standards of integrity in public service.","The chairperson said that she could not overemphasize the importance of maintaining the highest standards of integrity in public service, for it is only through the collective commitment of every government employee that they can hope to restore the people's trust.","The chairperson said that I cannot overemphasize the importance of maintaining the highest standards of integrity in public service."],"The chairperson said in her keynote address that she could not overemphasize the importance of maintaining the highest standards of integrity in public service, for it was only through the collective commitment of every government employee that they could hope to restore the people's trust in their institutions.","'Cannot' → 'could not'; 'is' → 'was'; 'can hope' → 'could hope'; 'I' → 'she'; 'we' → 'they'; 'our' → 'their.'",["tense backshift","modal verb","formal reporting"]))
ALL.append(q(499,"Hard",'CSE-style comprehensive: "I have been reliably informed that the funds that were supposed to have been released last quarter for the construction of the new government center have been diverted to other projects without the knowledge or consent of the local government unit concerned," the governor alleged in his privilege speech.',["The governor alleged in his privilege speech that he had been reliably informed that the funds that had been supposed to have been released the previous quarter for the construction of the new government center had been diverted to other projects without the knowledge or consent of the local government unit concerned.","The governor alleged that he has been reliably informed that the funds that were supposed to have been released last quarter have been diverted to other projects.","The governor alleged that he had been reliably informed that the funds that were supposed to have been released last quarter had been diverted to other projects without the knowledge or consent of the local government unit concerned.","The governor alleged that I have been reliably informed that the funds that were supposed to have been released last quarter have been diverted."],"The governor alleged in his privilege speech that he had been reliably informed that the funds that had been supposed to have been released the previous quarter for the construction of the new government center had been diverted to other projects without the knowledge or consent of the local government unit concerned.","'Have been informed' → 'had been informed'; 'were supposed' → 'had been supposed'; 'have been diverted' → 'had been diverted'; 'I' → 'he'; 'last quarter' → 'the previous quarter.'",["tense backshift","passive voice","time expression"]))
ALL.append(q(500,"Hard",'CSE-style comprehensive: "I solemnly swear that the testimony I am about to give is the truth, the whole truth, and nothing but the truth, and that I will answer all questions truthfully and to the best of my knowledge and recollection," the witness said before the tribunal.',["The witness said before the tribunal that he solemnly swore that the testimony he was about to give was the truth, the whole truth, and nothing but the truth, and that he would answer all questions truthfully and to the best of his knowledge and recollection.","The witness said that he solemnly swears that the testimony he is about to give is the truth, the whole truth, and nothing but the truth.","The witness said that he solemnly swore that the testimony he was about to give is the truth, the whole truth, and nothing but the truth, and that he will answer all questions truthfully.","The witness said that I solemnly swear that the testimony I am about to give is the truth."],"The witness said before the tribunal that he solemnly swore that the testimony he was about to give was the truth, the whole truth, and nothing but the truth, and that he would answer all questions truthfully and to the best of his knowledge and recollection.","'Swear' → 'swore'; 'am about to give' → 'was about to give'; 'is' → 'was'; 'will answer' → 'would answer'; 'I/my' → 'he/his.'",["tense backshift","formal reporting","compound sentence"]))

